 "text": " Imagine it is 2am. You have been typing a report for 3 hours without clicking save. Suddenly, the power cuts out. When you turn your computer back on, your old files are still sitting safely on your desktop. But those 3 hours of typing have vanished completely. Why did the old files survive while your open document disappeared? Welcome to Unit A of Team Doom's learning system. Even in Dr. Doom's automated foundries, computers are not magic boxes. There are physical machines governed by electricity. In the next few minutes, you will learn how a computer moves data between memory and processors, how simple zeros and ones run programs, and how sensors and circuits let hardware react to the real world.",
